WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.940
Picture a food truck that
costs $100,000 to set up.

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.420
In a good year, it earns
$20,000 of operating profit.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.240
That's its profit before
paying any interest.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:14.840
In a bad year, maybe it earns only $4,000.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:19.500
That's a year with a rainy
spring when few people but want

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.000
to buy lunch from an outdoor truck.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.980
The owners can borrow part of
the $100,000 from a bank at 8%

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:29.000
a year, and they put in
the rest of the capital

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:30.440
to start the truck themselves.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.780
So how does the size of the loan
change what the owners earn?

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.430
Well, the owners judge
the truck by their return

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.290
on their own money.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.790
Owner's return is operating
profit minus interest

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.090
divided by owner's money.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.230
Start with no loan at all.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.570
The owners put in the whole $100,000,

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:51.390
so there's no interest to pay.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:58.450
In a good year, $20,000 divided
by 100,000 is 0.2, or 20%.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.470
In a bad year, 4,000
divided by 100,000 is 4%.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.770
Now, what if they borrowed $20,000?

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.750
The owners put in the other $80,000.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:15.430
The interest is 20,000 times
8%, which is $1,600 a year.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.810
That interest is the same in
a good year or a bad year.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:22.430
The bank gets its $1,600, sun or rain.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:27.490
In the good year, 20,000 minus 1,600

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:29.870
leaves 18,400.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.670
Divided by 80,000, that's 23%.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:40.110
In the bad year, 4,000
minus 1,600 leaves 2,400.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.550
Divided by 80,000, that's 3%.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.410
The good year got a little better

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.510
and the bad year got a little worse.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.830
Now, what if the food truck
owners borrowed a lot of money,

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:52.890
$80,000?

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:56.150
The owners put in only $20,000.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.650
The interest is 80,000 times 8%,

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:05.670
which is $6,400 of interest
in a good year or a bad year.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:12.810
In the good year, $20,000
minus $6,400 leaves $13,600.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:17.130
Divided by the owners 20,000, that's 68%.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.650
In the bad year, the truck earns $4,000

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.290
but still owns the bank $6,400.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:29.430
4,000 minus 6,400 is minus 2,400.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:33.070
Divided by 20,000, that's minus 12%.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.410
The owners lose money and have to put up

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.330
more of their own money
just to repay the bank.

00:02:38.192 --> 00:02:41.642
Now, what if we let the
amount of the loan move?

00:02:42.392 --> 00:02:44.902
This chart shows the owner's
return for every loan

00:02:45.192 --> 00:02:47.122
from zero to $80,000.

00:02:47.732 --> 00:02:50.982
As the loan grows, the
good year return climbs

00:02:51.032 --> 00:02:52.502
and the bad year return sinks.

00:02:53.312 --> 00:02:54.682
The two lines fan apart.

00:02:55.392 --> 00:02:57.342
The bad year turns into a loss

00:02:57.392 --> 00:02:59.382
once the loan passes $50,000.

00:03:00.552 --> 00:03:03.882
At $50,000, the interest
is 50,000 times 8%,

00:03:03.932 --> 00:03:05.282
which is 4,000.

00:03:05.812 --> 00:03:07.702
That's everything we've
assumed the truck earns

00:03:07.752 --> 00:03:08.622
in a bad year.

00:03:09.283 --> 00:03:11.953
Why does more debt pull
the two years so far apart?

00:03:12.563 --> 00:03:14.393
First, the interest is the same

00:03:14.443 --> 00:03:15.873
in a good year and a bad one.

00:03:16.403 --> 00:03:19.793
The 6,400 comes off the top, sun or rain.

00:03:20.603 --> 00:03:22.793
Second, the owners put in less money,

00:03:23.323 --> 00:03:25.773
so each dollar of profit
or loss counts for more.

00:03:26.523 --> 00:03:29.013
With no loan, the owners make $20,000

00:03:29.103 --> 00:03:31.013
on 100,000 of their own money.

00:03:32.003 --> 00:03:36.893
With the $80,000 loan,
they make only $13,600,

00:03:37.643 --> 00:03:40.433
but they've only put up
$20,000 of their own money.

00:03:40.963 --> 00:03:43.533
That's fewer dollars, but
on a fifth of the money,

00:03:43.663 --> 00:03:46.653
so the return jumps from 20% to 68%,

00:03:46.703 --> 00:03:48.793
and the owners could have deployed

00:03:48.843 --> 00:03:51.493
their other $80,000 wherever they wanted,

00:03:51.923 --> 00:03:53.793
into the stock market or another business.

00:03:54.323 --> 00:03:56.273
That's how borrowing
makes a good year better

00:03:56.323 --> 00:03:57.693
and a bad year worse.
